  "method": [
    "Use the 434 x 432 source RGB raster before overlaid figure labels, with x rightward and y downward. The source image is fully opaque. Use the 12 MoS2 spots nearest radii 55 and 96 image pixels and the five unobscured bright first-ring hBN spots at radius about 70. Exclude the hBN spot crossed by the beam stop.",
    "At each green-channel level 115, 135 or 155 on the 8-bit RGB image, take the green-intensity weighted centroid of each connected spot. Output coordinates for 135 are given below.",
    "Read saved _xvec and _yvec coordinates and the _in_use mask in DS1 through DS14 diskset.pkl. Twelve in-use peaks make the two MoS2 rings. Begin from each of the six assignments of the first ring and both handedness conventions. For each assignment, match the twelve MoS2 peaks and fit an affine transformation including translation by ordinary least squares. Apply it to all remaining stored peak centers.",
    "Assign the five hBN source centers one-to-one to distinct unused archive peaks using minimum total Euclidean distance (linear_sum_assignment). Score their root mean square Euclidean separation and take its lowest value among the twelve conventions. The MoS2 RMS quoted alongside is from that same assignment.",
    "The comparison is a provenance check using different sets of diffraction spots. Source intensity levels and spot centers carry no fitted wall-model inputs. Absolute scan-to-crystal rotation is not obtained from this calculation."
  ],
