  "interpretation": "The source panel shows a strong recognizable hBN diffraction pattern, but it differs from the DS13/14 archived spot lists. The five-spot check gives subpixel agreement for the ten DS3 to DS12 controls. This rules out assigning the image as an independent angular reference for DS14 on the strength of the archive index. It does not identify the source acquisition uniquely or establish the true orientation of either target scan.",
